{
  "name": "Seafood Mixing",
  "code": "Log 049",
  "group": "Mixing Log",
  "scope": "line",
  "frequency": "Each batch",
  "description": "1. Record which product is being made. 2. Using a sanitized Thermapen, measure and record the temperature of the seafood mixture after mixing. 3. Record the time mixing was completed. 4. Record the time the batch is moved into production. 5. Record the batch temperature when it moves into production. 6. The time between every third batch feeding should be shorter than 4 hours. Seafood mix must be stored in the cooler with internal temperature ≤ 50°F; between 50–70°F it must be used within 5 hours. Sanitize the Thermapen before each use. Record when the last batch of the day enters production.",
